     "note": "THE LAST THREE UNPANELLED ROWS -- the final panel of a nine-panel campaign that took the backlog from 44 open single-seat rows to zero.\n\n*** THE SEATS SPLIT ON `tfreq` IN THE EXACT SHAPE THE BRIEF WARNED ABOUT, AND THE MEASUREMENT SETTLED IT. ***  agy and deepseek said tfreq is ALREADY FIXED and should be closed, not worked; minimax said do it FIRST, as a FIX+DETECTOR round. A direct contradiction about whether a defect still exists -- so it was CHECKED rather than voted.\n\nMEASURED, and it is decisive. BOTH write paths clamp before storing:\n  timer.c:130-136  '#427: clamp before anything is stored, so freq and interval agree' --\n                   freq = timer_clamp_freq(...) THEN newtimer->freq = freq.\n  timer_update_frequency()  '#427/#429: CLAMP FIRST, THEN compare, THEN store. The order is load-bearing and the shipped order was wrong twice over. THE OLD CODE STORED THE RAW VALUE INTO t->freq AND CLAMPED ONLY THE LOCAL, SO t->freq NAMED A RATE THE TIMER DID NOT RUN AT.'\nThat last sentence IS tfreq's title, in the source, marked fixed. tfreq is FIXED; its row is `active` with commits 863d238/b9daca1/cdc4849 and its hold says 'reviewed; regression batched to Sunday night'. It is awaiting a BATCHED REGRESS REVIEW, not open work.\n\nTHE SEAT-CLASS DOCTRINE PREDICTED THIS EXACTLY: the two seats that could OPEN THE FILE got it right; the packet-fed seat, reasoning from the row's text alone, would have sent a round at an already-closed defect. That is the fourth time in one night that a row's own text pointed the wrong way, and the second time a packet seat was overruled by one grep.\n\nes438: DROP AS A DEFECT ROW -- three seats (agy, deepseek, minimax), and agy's version is the useful one: CLOSE it as a completed review record while SPLITTING OUT the luna fuse-write defect it contains. A process record is not a defect row, but a real defect buried inside one must not be dropped with its container.\n\nrtcnarrow: deepseek would do it first. It is the design item filed earlier tonight, whose own three-device premise was already re-derived and largely dissolved.\n\nSeats: 6 of 7 (agy 9.5 KB, grok 9.8 KB, kimi 81.4 KB, glm 8.4 KB, deepseek 4.0 KB, minimax 12.3 KB). Codex ECHO-ONLY, ninth consecutive wall, proven arithmetically again: '21348b = brief 20660b + 688b'.\n\nFOR THIS ROW: *** MEASURED ALREADY FIXED -- close it, do not work it. ***  Two seats said so, one said do it FIRST, and the source settles it: both timer.c write paths clamp BEFORE storing, and timer_update_frequency's own comment states this row's title as the defect it fixed. The row is `active` with commits and its hold already says 'reviewed; regression batched to Sunday night' -- so it is awaiting its BATCHED REGRESS REVIEW, which is a queue position, not open work. NOT CLOSED HERE: codex-held, and a closure needs the full panel.",
