     "note": "OPTION A+C+D, and it BUILT THE INSTRUMENT rather than judging its feasibility. Compiled an offline differential of memory_rw.c on the first attempt and reproduced the defect immediately -- the key being that memory_rw.c has no PPC/ARM/SH flavour, so compiling with NO family macro excludes the MIPS/M88K/Alpha branches and leaves 4 headers, 3 globals and 6 stubs. Then MEASURED a four-variant table that settled the round: Option B is not a fix (a straddle beginning in a device still returns d0 d0 00 00); A alone SIGSEGVs on a 256 MB access because gcc does NOT turn the tail recursion into a loop at -O2 (~160 B/page); D is free and keeps the memblock split load-bearing. Also found TWO consequences the brief had missed: a straddling WRITE leaves the intended page unmodified and alters an unrelated one, and a faulting tail returned MEMORY_ACCESS_OK -- a missing fault. Verified the live trees untouched afterwards by md5.",
