     "note": "HOLD, and it was RIGHT to hold -- this is the seat that caught the granule. It produced the 1 KB counterexample (a four-byte read at 0x13fe crosses a translation boundary but not a 4 KB one) with the three tree citations that make it real: memory_arm.c's non-XScale descriptor type 3, memory_sh.c's SH4_PTEL_SZ_1K, and the VR41xx path. Also found that splitting broke #244's whole-buffer zero promise, and that `offset + len` can wrap. All three fixed. Notably it ANSWERED NORMALLY on this brief after being content-flagged on the pass-1 brief two hours earlier -- same subject, neutral bounds-correctness wording.",
