   "hold": "R7 - the trailing-garbage half only",
   "witness": "none -- host-side only, same caller census as [[b118]]. A build is needed to run the parse, though the reading is unambiguous.",
   "state_note": "*** EVIDENCE 2026-08-27: TRUE, host-side only. The other half of `#414`'s residual -- see [[b118]]. ***\n\n`src/disk/diskimage.c:1693` and `:1698` call `strtoll(fname, NULL, 10)` -- **NULL endptr, so the stop position is discarded** -- and the loops at `:1694` and `:1699` then skip *any* bytes until `;` or `:`. Trailing text after the digits is consumed silently: `g16abc;63:` and `g16;63abc:` both parse as 16/63.\n\n**This is an INCOMPLETE conversion, not an unconverted site.** `#414` replaced `atoi` with `strtoll` at these two fields precisely to fix a parsing defect (`:1681-1687`, *'turning g010 into 8 heads'*) -- but passing `NULL` for the endptr threw away the one thing `strtoll` offers over `atoi` for this purpose.\n\nA seat also noted a secondary host-only effect worth keeping: with letters after S, `g16;63b:` never sets the boot prefix, because the skip loop swallows them.\n\n**NOT guest-reachable** -- same two startup callers as [[b118]].\n\n"
  },
