     "note": "REAL - the TSTR arm never reads timer_hz[], which only the TCR arm writes; the struct is memset so step=(uint32_t)(0.0/110.0)=0 and TCNT never moves - a timer the guest believes it started, frozen for ever. SECOND freeze mode on the same line: any timer_hz < 110.0 truncates to 0. HONEST UNKNOWN: whether OpenBSD writes TSTR before TCR was not booted, only that nothing prevents or reports it. Precedent for the missing guard: pclock==0 exits loudly at :1236-1240.",
