     "note": "TRUE AS CODE, DEAD AS DEFECT. `d` is linked at diskimage.c:1822-1830 and six later failure paths return -1 with it still linked (:1964, :1980, :1991, :2074, :2088, :2099); the first three leave d->f == NULL. BUT THERE ARE EXACTLY TWO CALL SITES AND BOTH ABORT THE PROCESS -- emul_parse.c:558 -> exit(1) at :561, and main.c:707 -> 'Aborting.' and return 1 from main() at :709. VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY BY THE MAIN LOOP at both sites. Nothing ever consumes the broken entry. Recommend DROP AS A ROUND, keep as a rider on the next diskimage round, and re-promote immediately if a third non-aborting caller appears. Minor extra: the :2099 path leaks tmpname/tmpname.map in /tmp where :2088 unlinks.  [panel_20260817_174701]",
