th is correct only by coincidence at alloc==191. The true value is not known at :607 because the page is written later at :630+, so the write must MOVE AFTER the pagecode switch.\n* BLAST RADIUS: nothing reads retlen after :607 (next use :746 is an assignment in the READ case), and data_in[0] is read NOWHERE outside diskimage_scsicmd.c across all of src/ -- every HBA sizes from data_in_len, so the guest is the only consumer. No overflow: max write is q+29 = 45 against a >=100-byte buffer.\n* DETECTOR built and feasible offline. TWO DESIGN POINTS THAT MATTER: the rows MUST SPAN PAGES {0,1,3,4,5}, because every page-4 case has true_len 36 and a mutant hardcoding 35 would pass a page-4-only test; and an INVARIANCE row -- the reported length must not vary with the allocation length -- NAMES THE DEFECT RATHER THAN A VALUE, so a '+100 -> +0' half-fix cannot pass it. -ffunction-sections/-Wl,--gc-sections is required or mymkstemp/debug_indentation fail to link.\n* ADJACENT, measured en route: MODE SENSE(10) writes the 6-BYTE header layout, so a conformant guest parses block_desc_len=0 while 8 real descriptor bytes sit at offset 8 -- STRICTLY WORSE than b120r, and unreached today only because no rig issues MS10. And data_in_len is set to the FULL allocation length even when far less data exists (alloc 255 -> 255 bytes, 219 of them zeros) where a real drive transfers 36, which affects residual logic.\n* HONEST UNKNOWN, stated by the seat: three guests measured, ALL OpenBSD. Whether a NetBSD/Ultrix/Linux driver asks an allocation length in [156,190] was not measured.\n* It also caught a citation error of mine: REQUEST SENSE forcing is :964-967, not the :957-960 my brief claimed. Verified and corrected above.  [agent b120r 2026-08-19]"
