     "note": "REAL AS A SHAPE, CORRECTLY FILED AS DESIGN, AND NOT WORTH A ROUND -- close as a standing note. timer.h:84 timer_add(double freq,...) has NO one-shot form at all; footbridge reads a FREERUN/PERIODIC bit (dc21285reg.h:365-366) and ignores it, reload_timer_value (:224-248) always installs a repeating timer, and the TIMER_1_CLEAR distinction at :590 is a no-op because timer_update_frequency early-outs on an unchanged freq (timer.c:204). The author's own comment at :250-256 admits it. BUT THE DANGEROUS HALF IS ALREADY FIXED (#427's timer_clamp_freq turned the guest-writable zero divisor -> +INF -> 0.0 interval -> in-handler hang into a bounded rate), so what remains is pure fidelity. AND IT HAS NO WITNESS OF EITHER KIND: none of the four bootable rigs (pmax, arc, luna88k, landisk) instantiates an ISA bus or a footbridge. Self-corrected mid-analysis: nearly asserted the 8253 is instantiated by nothing, but it is reachable via bus_isa.c:241 -- just not from a rig we can boot.  [panel_20260817_174701]"
