     "note": "VERDICT ROUND.  Existing floors (section U's 30-pin manifest, GATE_MANIFEST=16, check_probe_wiring's UNWIRED DETECTOR) catch SOME whole-block deletions: deleting gate_offline.sh's absorb selftest or gate_ppc.sh's rlwimi block is caught; deleting gate_offline.sh's absorb-CONTROL block (143-181) leaves every checker's output unchanged -- measured in memory.  Cheapest floor: a committed per-gate census of check/check_min source sites (prototype 346 -> 342 on the deletion, exit 1; growth also red).  ALSO FOUND A LIVE DEFECT IN THE #529 WORKING SET: the pin label `crime width rows run' is invisible to check_score_claims.py's one-token PIN regex (PINNED 29 vs manifest 30) while its gate comment said the regex saw it -- fixed the same hour (stem `crime_width')."
    }
