     "note": "*** TRUE, AND ITS 'ZERO SEAT ENTRIES' IS A LEDGER ARTIFACT, NOT AN UNASSESSED ITEM. *** OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:2698+ ALREADY HOLDS THE FULL ANALYSIS -- verified independently by the main loop, which found the existing text naming the same mechanism. Re-verified the mechanism anyway: cpu_arm_instr.c:1550 fast path does p32[(addr & 0xfff) >> 2] (the >>2 truncates addr[1:0], which IS the architectural answer) while :1563 slow path hands raw addr to memory_rw -- same instruction, two answers, selected by PAGE RESIDENCY. Thumb PUSH/POP inherits it (cpu_arm.c:1670,1677). AND IT RE-CHECKED THE ARM CITATIONS AGAINST THE REAL LOCAL MANUAL, all three holding: LDM(1) p.A4-37, STM(1) p.A4-190, Table A2-10 'Operation unaffected by Addr[1:0]' p.A2-40 -- its own first grep reported them unverifiable and that was ITS error, caught by re-grepping. Relabel: ANALYSED AND READY, not unassessed.  [panel_20260817_174701]"
