    {
     "phase": "research",
     "seat": "opus5",
     "date": "2026-08-19",
     "verdict": "REAL",
     "evidence": "CONFIRMED",
     "note": "*** REPRODUCED, AND THE FIX IS MEASURED RATHER THAN ARGUED. *** Probe built on the testarm/SA1110 cold debugger with a four-byte raw stub; every encoding re-verified through the emulator's own unassemble before any row was believed. Three binaries in a private tree:\n* HEAD scores 9/15 rows against the architecture; MASK AT THE ACCESS scores 15/15; MASK AT ENTRY scores 14/15 and CORRUPTS THE BASE WRITEBACK (0x00070004 for 0x00070006). *** #357's 'mask at entry corrupts the writeback' is REAL, NOT FOLKLORE -- the mutant was built and measured. ***\n* The divergence, three ways: the SAME LDM run twice against one page returns 0x77881122 then 0x11223344; ONE LDM WITH TWO REGISTERS returns r1 from a raw unaligned address and r3 from an aligned one -- MIXED WITHIN A SINGLE INSTRUCTION, because r1's own access warmed the page; and a cold STM SPILLS INTO THE NEXT WORD (0x00FF3344 / 0x5566FFFF).\n* IT SIDESTEPPED THE `put w` WARMS / `put b` DOES NOT TRAP RATHER THAN TRUSTING IT: the slow path's own memory_rw inserts the page on its way out (memory_rw.c:732, no NO_EXCEPTIONS), so the first bdt access to a cold page is slow and every later one is fast. Running the IDENTICAL instruction twice makes the divergence a difference between two executions rather than a value that depends on trusting a seeding rule.\n* FIX: two lines, cpu_arm_instr.c:1563 (load) and :1752 (store), addr -> addr & ~(uint32_t)3. Confirmed from the CODE (`uint32_t addr = *np` at :1514, `if (w_bit) *np = addr` at :1624 -- addr IS the writeback value), from the LOCAL manual (A5.4.2 p.A5-43; LDM(1) p.A4-37, STM(1) p.A4-190), and from the ENTRY mutant. NUANCE it caught: the Multi-word row of Table A2-10 is on the CONTINUATION page A2-41, not A2-40 where the table starts.\n* IN-TREE PRECEDENT it did not expect: generate_arm_multi.c:117 already emits `addr &= 0xffc` and the generated combiners write back from the UNMASKED register -- upstream's own generated LDM combiners already use exactly this shape, and they fall back to instr(bdt_load) on a cold page, so they inherit both the defect and the fix. Thumb PUSH/POP (cpu_arm.c:1670,1677) call the same two functions; arm_pop/arm_push have exactly four callers, all enumerated.\n* *** THE EXISTING GATE IS BLIND TO IT, MEASURED: arm_writeback_probe.py scores 22/22 on ALL THREE binaries including the ENTRY mutant that corrupts the writeback, and gate 14's 261 checks touch neither arm_pop nor arm_push. *** The single check separating the correct fix from the #357 trap is the W=1 writeback row. So the gate row is NOT redundant and must land in the SAME commit as the fix, being scored against architecture rather than against HEAD.\n* Side effect named rather than left to be found: masking also removes the 4 KB page-straddle path for bdt, where a raw access at P+0xFFE currently translates once and takes its tail from the physical continuation.\n* It also caught a records defect against the main loop: _scratchpad/CHECKPOINT.md had gone stale, naming HEAD 4d0981d and 'Tree CLEAN' when HEAD was 9bcae1c and two files were uncommitted. Re-derived.  [agent armbdt 2026-08-19]"
    },
