     "ev": "regress/artifacts/armbdt/killtable_20260911f_opus/SCORES.txt + probe_*.raw + ldmdb_*.out (preserved from /tmp BEFORE this record cited them, with drivers/).  Every probe_*.raw ends ARMBDT_WITNESS_DONE -- no truncation.  94 tool uses, 26m.  Built EIGHT legs in its own clone, baseline named as 8d372aa and cmp'd, rm *.o + [binary -nt source] per leg, clone restored and deleted.",
     "note": "*** A MEASUREMENT, NOT A READING. FIVE clause-(d) mutants at 32/32 -- a TOTAL ESCAPE EACH. ***\n    M_POPP_NONE   p_bit ? addr : (addr & 0xfffffffc)          32/32\n    M_POPP_WEAK   addr & (p_bit ? 0xfffffffe : 0xfffffffc)    32/32   (codex+grok predicted this one)\n    M_POPW_WEAK   addr & (w_bit ? 0xfffffffe : 0xfffffffc)    32/32\n    M_SBIT_NONE   s_bit ? addr : (addr & ~3)  BOTH sites      32/32\n    M_NPMASK      (*np) & 0xfffffffc -- mask on the WRONG operand  32/32\n\n**`M_POPP_NONE` IS THE SHARPEST: it is not a subtle weakening, it is CLAUSE (b) -- the removed\ndefect reinstated VERBATIM -- restricted to `p_bit == 1`, and the detector cannot see it.**\n\n*** NON-EQUIVALENCE CONTROL RUN, so 'the target is dead' is EXCLUDED rather than assumed. ***\n`LDMDB r0!,{r1}` = `0xe9300002`, r0 = 0x2000a, access 0x20006 (`ldmdb_*.out`):\n    BASE          r1 = 0x55667788  ok      M_POPP_NONE  r1 = 0x00005566  FAIL\n    M_POPW_WEAK   r1 = 0x00005566  FAIL    M_NPMASK     r1 = 0x00000000  FAIL\nwith the writeback r0 = 0x00020006 CORRECT on all four.  **Three escaping mutants CORRUPT A GUEST\nREGISTER on an instruction the detector never issues**, each returning exactly the value its\narithmetic predicts -- and `M_POPP_NONE`'s 0x00005566 is the FIX-ABSENT value, i.e. the pre-fix\ndefect returning.  Reachability is not a corner case: none of these encodings is in the 256-entry\n`cpu_arm_multi.txt` fast list, and `cpu_arm_instr.c:4810-4811` disables the optimised path entirely\nfor a BIG-ENDIAN guest, so on BE **every** block transfer goes through the patched helpers.\n\n**THE CLASS, in its own words:** *\"Every p/u/s/w partition is discharged on the STORE side and\nundischarged on the LOAD side, because the only leg that varies any of those bits is Thumb PUSH --\nwhich calls arm_push. arm_pop is driven at exactly ONE (p,u,s) point, (0,1,0).\"*  **And it is a\nbreach of the round's OWN enumeration:** `PRETABLE3.out` declares the space as {site} x {residue} x\n{word position} x {p_bit} and says *\"close every cell in ONE diff\"* -- it then honoured {site} for\n`M_MASK7` (adding BOTH the LDM and STM BIT2 rows) and did NOT honour it for `p_bit`, adding only\n`THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2`.  Three cells of a two-by-two.\n\n*Missable for a structural reason worth keeping: the load-side cell CANNOT be closed by copying the\npush row -- the probe's only p_bit=1 caller is Thumb PUSH, so closing {load}x{p_bit=1} needs a NEW\nINSTRUCTION WORD (LDMIB/LDMDB), not a new base.*\n\nTHE BRIEF'S OWN CANDIDATE `& ~15` **DIES** (M_MASK15 30/32), and `M_MASK1` reproduced\n`killtable_20260911e` exactly (29/32) -- so the rig rebuilds and the probe discriminates.\n\nIT ALSO FOUND `THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2` IS THE **SOLE CARRIER** OF THE WHOLE p_bit AXIS (an L3\nshape), reads through the freshly-repaired `read_mem32`, and asserts ONE half where its sibling\n`ARM_STM_COLD_DATA_BIT2` asserts two -- adding `w1 == 0` is free.\n\nRECOMMENDED CLOSURE, one diff: LDM IB/DA/DB/S at residue 2 with DATA oracles, plus\n`LDMIA r0!,{r1,r2}` from +2 -- **one leg, three assertions, kills M_POPW_WEAK AND M_NPMASK and\ncloses the w_bit x residue-2 and reg-list-length axes together**; mirror on the store side.  And\nthe repair owes its own pass: passes A, B and C each found a breach."
