     "note": "166,801 b -- *** THE CLI SEAT IS BACK (it was walled at 350 b all day) AND IT MEASURED, NOT READ. *** Built five NEW escapes at 39/39 in its own clone (/tmp/gx524d, frozen probe, fresh binary per leg, restore cmp CLEAN): E1 M_PUSHS_NONE (s_bit at PUSH only -- the push half of pass C's own M_SBIT_NONE, which was built both-sites and observed only on the load side); E2 M_POPSW_WEAK ((s&&w) at POP -- the only s=1 load row has w=0); E3 M_POPS_OVER7 (s ? ~7 : ~3 -- S_P2's access 0x20002 has bit 2 CLEAR, where ~7 and ~3 AGREE); E4 M_PUSHP_OVER7 (p ? ~7 : ~3 at PUSH -- Thumb PUSH's accesses are bit2-clear); E5 M_PUW_WEAK ((p&&u&&w) BOTH sites -- no row drives p=u=w=1). **CALIBRATION KILLS prove the sweep can see kills**: M_PU_WEAK_BOTH 38/39 and M_W_OVER7_BOTH 38/39 -- so BOTH mutants I had disclosed as unbuilt do NOT escape, which retires that disclosure. *** AND IT FOUND ONE OF MY CLOSURE ROWS VACUOUS BY CONSTRUCTION: ARM_LDM_MULTI_P2_R2 cannot fail under a slow-path mutant because THE FIRST COLD ACCESS WARMS THE PAGE and the second register's access takes the FAST path. *** I had disclosed it as 'kills nothing'; the real reason is structural and worse."
