     "d": "SPLIT-REFUTED-FLOOR-IS-10-CELLS",
     "date": "2026-09-11",
     "grade": "CONFIRMED",
     "ev": "regress/artifacts/armbdt/passD/fable_floor_20260911.md -- adjudication fired LAST, after all 7 scriptable seats answered pass D.  Liveness proven (token + verbatim CHECKPOINT line).  28 tool uses, 306k tokens.",
     "note": "*** REFUTED MY SPLIT IN BOTH HALVES ON A CATEGORY SLIP I MADE: the joint-cell rule's 'body' is the GUARDED BODY -- the cold `else` branch -- not the enclosing function. ***  My grep found p/u/s/w tested in `arm_pop`/`arm_push`; the guarded body of the pop edit (`:1652-1730`) tests exactly two things, the `memory_rw` return and `cpu->byte_order`.  So the JOIN rule governs and it is ASYMMETRIC: p,u flow into `addr` (FLOOR both sites); s reaches nothing on pop but flows into `value` -> `data` on push (FLOOR on push, (e) on pop); w reaches nothing at either site ((e)); `i == ARM_PC` flows into `value = cpu->pc + 12` on push (FLOOR on push).  **AND p/u ARE ONE SELECTOR WITH FOUR VALUES -- the addressing mode**: the code nests the tests, the architecture names the pair as one field, and `generate_arm_multi.c:120` switches on `p*2+u`.  So `(p && u)` is not a joint, it is the cell IB -- and THE STORE SIDE IS MISSING TWO WHOLE MODES, since STM rows are IA and Thumb PUSH is hardcoded DB (`cpu_arm.c:1670`).  FLOOR = {cold first access} x {pop,push} x {IA,IB,DA,DB} + {push}x{s=1} + {push}x{pc in list} = TEN CELLS, one cold DATA row each at an access address = 7 (mod 8).  Seven open.  My five E-mutants regrade: E1 FLOOR (L2, measured); E2/E3/E5 clause (e); E4 (e) but closes free.  **My bound was wrong on three counts: w is not an axis, `~2` is missing from the strength set, and p/u are one selector.**  THE `~2` GAP IS LIVE: all three closure rows access `0x20006` with bit 0 CLEAR, so `addr & (p_bit ? 0xfffffffd : 0xfffffffc)` escapes by arithmetic -- my residue-3 disclosure went false the moment pass C admitted mode-conditioning.  *** ON CONVERGENCE: NOT `#392`. ***  Regraded under the correct floor the counts are 1, 1, 3, 1 -- not 1, 2, 5, 5; **the rising count was DEBT GRADED AS FLOOR**.  The other growth is the `#499` shape: every repair placed rows at the FOUND MUTANT'S residue instead of enumerating from the function's inputs -- pass C invoked the class-closure amendment and then executed it FROM THE MUTANT LIST, which the probe's own comment admits.  **The geometric fix is one line: put every row at residue 7 mod 8, where `~1`, `~2`, `~3` and `~7` are discriminated AT ONCE.**  Disposition: ONE closing diff then ONE verifying pass; not ship-now (E1 corrupts guest memory under a legal STM(2)), not hold-indefinitely."
    },
