     "note": "*** THE CLI SEAT IS BACK. *** It was walled at 350 b all day (a SEAT FAILURE, covered by the kimi-k3:cloud substitute) and returned 169,752 b on pass D -- and it MEASURED rather than read, building five escapes in its own clone with calibration kills. The substitute answered the same panel at 7,923 b and is PACKET-FED, so it may not be credited with any repo fact the CLI seat could read. Recording both separately is the sixth seat-failure class working as intended: a walled CLI with a live substitute is ONE SEAT COVERED, never one seat lost -- and when both answer, that is two answers."
