   "hold_question": "DISCHARGED 2026-08-29 -- both parts answered (see the 2026-08-29 entry): the MASKED path is right, controlling text LDM(1) A4-37 / STM(1) A4-190 re-verified from the local manual, and the ranking is above b120r. The question's own A4-44 premise was REFUTED. WHAT REMAINS: the rung-3 probe is private and uncommitted with no artifact under regress/, so the reproduction cannot be re-verified by anyone -- that is the open item, and it is a durable-artifact gap rather than a reasoning one. (Prior question text, kept as provenance: ARM block transfer: the two paths disagree about an unaligned base. QUESTION, two parts. (a) WHICH PATH IS RIGHT? Answer from DDI 0100I and cite the page you actually read -- this project has shipped ARM page numbers that came from panel output rather than a manual, and `_scratchpad/ddi0100i.txt` is)",
   "note": "*** COMMITTED 2026-09-12 as 4dfc716 (local only).  gate 14 PASS 910 checks at the 43 pin (regress/artifacts/armbdt/killtable_20260911h_floor/gate_arm_43rows.log); all four trees cleared both parts after cpu_arm_instr.c was propagated (three trees held an older comment).  Pass-2 receipt in regress/pass2_ledger.tsv.  State stays `held`: the closure records are owed. ***\n\n*** GATE PIN RAISED 39 -> 43 (2026-09-12).  THE GATE MUST BE RE-RUN; ITS LAST GREEN WAS AT 39. ***\n\nTable 7 added four rows to close the floor -- the three store-side modes that had NO ROW AT ALL\n(`ARM_STM_IB_R7`, `ARM_STM_DA_R7`, `ARM_STM_S_R7`) and the tenth cell (`ARM_STM_PC_DB_R7`) -- so\nthe probe is 43 rows and the literal moved by hand with its reason.  **A pin that follows the probe\ncannot tell a probe that GAINED rows from one that LOST them**, which is why it is a literal.\n\nOWED FOR `#524`, IN ORDER:\n  1. re-run `gate_arm.sh` at the 43 pin;\n  2. re-add the `arm_bdt_probe.py` MANIFEST entry to `check_probe_wiring.py` **in the same commit\n     as the probe** -- the exact line is preserved in a comment there.  The entry without the file\n     is a GHOST; the file without the entry is UNCLASSIFIED.  Both are red, in opposite\n     directions, and I hit each in turn today;\n  3. restore the `#524` CHANGELOG block (`python _scratchpad/land_shared.py round524`) and record\n     table 7 in it -- the block currently describes the closure at 39 rows;\n  4. commit, AFTER `#525`.\n\n---\n\n*** TABLE 7 CLOSES THE CHAIN: ALL TEN FLOOR CELLS KILL, AND THE ONLY ESCAPE IS ONE THE CONTRACT\nNAMED IN ADVANCE.  2026-09-12 02:32. ***  Cited: regress/artifacts/armbdt/killtable_20260911h_floor/SCORES.txt\n\n    BASE            43/43  CONTROL=OK  FAILING none\n    -- regression, the six from table g: all still die --\n    M_POPP_NONE     41/43  IB_P2, DB_P2         M_POPP_WEAK  41/43  IB_P2, DB_P2\n    M_NPMASK        41/43  IB_P2, DB_P2         M_SBIT_NONE  (dies)\n    M_POPW_WEAK     40/43  DB_P2, S_P2, MULTI_P2_R1          M_POPU_WEAK  (dies)\n    -- the six NEW floor mutants: ALL DIE --\n    M_PUSHS_NONE    42/43  ARM_STM_S_R7          <- E1, the MEASURED L2 breach\n    M_POPP_MASK2    41/43  IB_P2, DB_P2          <- the ~2 gap, live until residue 7\n    M_PUSH_IB_WEAK  42/43  ARM_STM_IB_R7         <- a mode with NO ROW AT ALL\n    M_PUSH_DA_WEAK  42/43  ARM_STM_DA_R7         <- likewise\n    M_PUSHPC_NONE   42/43  ARM_STM_PC_DB_R7      <- the tenth cell\n    M_PUSHP_OVER7   41/43  ARM_STM_IB_R7, ARM_STM_PC_DB_R7   <- E4\n    -- disclosed under clause (e), EXPECTED to escape --\n    D_PUW_WEAK      43/43  FAILING none          <- ESCAPED, exactly as disclosed\n    D_POPSW_WEAK    42/43  ARM_LDM_S_P2          <- DIED, better than disclosed\n    RESTORE
