   "id": "ramspaninval",
   "title": "OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:2727-2728 at db8b1a33 -- a bulk RAM write invalidates translated code once per memblock fragment, at the fragment's first page (memory_rw.c:760; the split and recursion at :762-775), so translated code in the later pages it writes can go stale -- CONDITIONAL: only an access that skips the 1 KB split (a PHYSICAL access, or a CPU with no translate_v2p: memory_rw.c:186) reaches that single invalidate with a length past its first page, e.g. GD-ROM DMA on the Dreamcast; a translated store is cut to at most 1024 bytes and each chunk invalidates its own page.  The queue's prose says `only the endpoint pages`",
