   "state_note": "FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 ('#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors'), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :169 (DREG read, phase outside DATAIN/STAT/MSGIN) and :235 (DREG write, phase outside DATAOUT/CMD).  :290 (the end-of-write default:) is UNREACHABLE: the first switch returns only for unsupported phases, and DATAOUT/CMD break, reach the second switch with no intervening phase change, and exhaust its supported cases.  PREREQUISITES: every DREG helper call needs a NONZERO count before decrement (a zero-count access only warns) and these guards additionally need a transfer object -- 'unconditional' means independent of the abort flag, nothing more.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): SCMD/PCTL give the guest control of the phase.  FIX SHAPE: keep the CPU running while KEEPING the helper's early return (:170 / :236) -- the treatment #186 gave the XFR command at :507.  PROVENANCE: agy's ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -> GPT-6 Astra's finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu->running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -> grok's ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -> Astra's confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.",
