   "state_note": "FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 ('#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors'), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :312 (len != 1: a halfword or word callback access), :533 (an SCMD WRITE outside {0x00, 0x20, 0x84, 0x8c, 0xc0} unless bit 0x10 rewrites it to BUS_REL -- an SCMD read does not execute this switch), and EXBF, register index 15: WRITE logging at :676 and READ logging at :683 converge on the ONE assignment at :690.  All gated by const bool mb89352_abort_on_unimplemented_stuff = true (:61), so live; the shared fixed-true policy is what groups them.  REACHED BY (by reading, not measured): those accesses from the guest's register interface.  FIX SHAPE: the warning branch the flag already selects; clearing the flag leaves all five live unconditional DREG assignments (:146, :169, :176, :235, :242; :290 is dead) intact.  NOT mb89352halt's stop: that dropped row's record names the disk dispatcher's CDB default: and the controller's status-length guard, not :533.  PROVENANCE: agy's ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -> GPT-6 Astra's finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu->running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -> grok's ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -> Astra's confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.",
