   "state_note": "FILED BY #558 from queue passage 2616 at db8b1a33 ('#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors'), which #555 gave ONE row (qhm88kstops, dev_mb89352.c:146).  SITES (c29a5fd3, src/devices/dev_mb89352.c): :176 (DREG read, transfer_bufpos >= len against the selected DATAIN, STAT or MSGIN buffer -- read completion changes phase WITHOUT resetting the cursor, so a subsequent nonempty buffer can meet this guard, not only the original DATAIN buffer) and :242 (DREG write: reachable through empty or unprepared outgoing-buffer states; an exact fill runs completion and can change phase so a further write reaches :235 instead).  PREREQUISITES: a transfer object and a nonzero count, as for the phase guards (the count prerequisite applies to every DREG helper call; the :146 stop is the case with NO transfer object).  CARRIERS OF THE REST: b120 carries the unknown-CDB producer omission and its empty-status consequence; this row's residual is every OTHER empty-buffer path and every nonempty-buffer case.  FIX SHAPE: keep the bounds protection and refuse the access or handle phase completion -- removing the guard exposes the indexed accesses at :180 / :246 -- a CONTROLLER fix; b120 remains the PRODUCER fix.  PROVENANCE: agy's ifiled2_1 flag #27 (PARTLY) -> GPT-6 Astra's finding that the title carries one of nine `cpu->running = 0` assignments (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_agyflags/codex_aconf_agyflags.txt) -> grok's ruling, CONCEDE IN PART, three rows (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/grok/grok_mbstops.txt) -> Astra's confirmation (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/aconf_mbstops/codex_aconf_mbstops.txt: CONFIRMED WITH CHANGES (3) -- correct reachability explanations, qualify carrier/title scope, and label evidence as source-only; retain three HIGH rows).  Severity HIGH by the qhm88kstops grade (a guest-drivable stop of the emulated CPU).  Reachability established by source inspection at c29a5fd3; no runtime witness measured -- the round that takes this row owes the rung-3 attempt.  NOT FIXED by #558.",
