  {
   "id": "closeassessrows",
   "title": "the 2026-08-27 sweep closed CLOSE (assess) rows that still name undone work, and each member needs a re-open decision",
   "sev": "MED",
   "state": "open",
   "opened": "2026-10-02",
   "commits": "",
   "witness": "",
   "hold_question": "",
   "state_note": "[2026-10-02] THE CENSUS (#557): grok read the 37 closed-no-commit rows no seat had read (regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/grok/grok_closedcensus.txt): 20 shipped, 14 nothing owed, 3 work still alive.  Astra confirmed 34 and overturned 3 (regress/artifacts/closeassess_20261002/aconf_census/codex_aconf_census.txt): boilerplateprefix and smhang moved from shipped to alive (smhang's timeout shipped and its standing regression did not; boilerplateprefix's repair was uncommitted), gdromcontractresidual re-scoped.  So: 17 commits fields filled from the twenty (smhang's among them, for the part that shipped) plus xfamscope's, read before the census -- 18 fills; 2 left empty on purpose (asanunbuildable, wiringshghost); boilerplateprefix's filled by the post step with #557's own sha; 14 nothing owed; 5 work still alive -- 4 added as members below, the fifth, boilerplateprefix, landed by #557 itself.  boilerplateprefix and smhang are in both the shipped twenty and the alive five, which is why those three counts sum past 37.  FILLING THE FIELDS BROUGHT THE ROWS UNDER SECTIONS K AND I FOR THE FIRST TIME (the 19:10 precheck): 3 witness fields added and 2 re-shaped, 8 regress reviews held with their questions -- K's witness-presence rule and I's missing-regress rule both key on the commits field, so a closed-with-no-commit row escapes exactly those two (the same precheck also found #556's hrecordowed unattributed, section L, a separate leftover).  MEMBERS NOW (12): m8latch, gcsections, ns16550, pcchalt, wdcstandby, rtcnarrow, scunbacked, m437multi, cmtattr, gdromcontractresidual, smhang, unreadseats23.  A CLASS ROW (a records defect of the ledger).  MEMBERS (8): m8latch, gcsections, ns16550, pcchalt, wdcstandby, rtcnarrow, scunbacked, m437multi.  READ BY NO SEAT (2), closed by the same sweep with no commit: ledgerwitness, cmtattr.  Nothing is re-opened by this row: the audit of each member -- re-open, re-file, or close with a commit -- is its work.  The ruling seat's evidence (grok/grok_grok_irule_d.txt 5 (conceding in part; Astra's ifile_04 raised it)): `CLOSE (assess)` signs off the assess stage. The seven rows whose notes continue past it are still live: `i8253zero` held (`ledger.json:9278`), `idesync` in work (`:12953`), `wdcflood` in work (`:13498`), `landiskdisk` in work (`:13993`), `rtcflood` held (`:15096`), `floodclass` held (`:15480`), `isaorder` held (`:16315`). The sweep's own text, `ledger.json:10393`, closed the bare note and performed no re-check. Eleven is too many. Checked and still undone, with no later carrier: `m8latch` (`dev_m8820x.c:90-97`), `gcsections` (`gate_offline.sh:729`, `:820`), `ns16550` (`dev_ns16550.c:181`), `pcchalt` (no `regress/ppc*.py` page-crossing probe; halt comment only at `cpu_ppc_instr_loadstore.c:63-84`), `wdcstandby` (`WDCC_STANDBY_IMMED` is `0xe0` at `wdcreg.h:138` and still hits `default:` with `WDCE_ABRT` at `dev_wdc.c:1155-1156`), `rtcnarrow` (`dev_vr41xx.c:606` integer-divides `RTCL1_L_HZ / idata` and `:614` ignores the high half; `ledger.json:15084` says the core floor is the wrong fix site), `scunbacked` (`gate_offline.sh:2346-2349` still greps bare `@@SELFCHECK@@` while `diff_rtc_range.c:140` names that token in a comment), `m437multi` (`diskimage.c:1291-1292` still writes only the last overlay, and `:2395-2412` fails the sync if any overlay fsync fails). Checked and left out: `m8sarseq` is carried by open `m8sarrows` (`ledger.json:25702-25704`); `xfamscope`'s two edits are in `gate_crossfamily.sh:173-193` and `:207-218`; `m437rtmp` owes no code, and its scope statement is `OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md:5806-5810` with the `R:` unlink at `diskimage.c:177-182`. One carrier, and this ruling does not re-open the closed rows. Passages 1-3 point here. Passage 4 does not.",
   "entries": [
