probes install breakpoints and breakpoints disable read-ahead. || qhstrlenbilling -- strlen probe cannot check 3n-1 billing closer than about 8K || qhcpycoldremeas -- cold-source memcpy fold count is unreconciled and still queued for re-measurement || qhcpybailrate -- Owed real-guest measurement of the memcpy bail rate, including silent zero-iteration bails. || qhcpybillmeas -- Owed measurement of whether the -J arm and the marker arms agree on instruction billing. || qhcpytailcov -- memcpy probe has no two-iteration tail row at word 16 || qhcpydumpdiag -- memcpy probe treats a short dump as a bad destination word || qhcpysamplecov -- memcpy probe samples five destination words and misses a 7-of-8 copy || qhbatchcounter -- the guest mp counter includes the dyntrans batch quantum of 120 || qhstepbranch -- Owed observation of a step onto a fold slot reached as a branch target, under the source-derived expectation of uncombined execution. || qhusertlbmeas -- Owed measurement of is_userpage across TLB eviction, recording that invalidation clears the bit. || qhcpycountcov -- memcpy marker-count times 32 is unchecked against the r0 advance || qhfireexact -- copyin and copyout fires rows accept any positive marker count || qharmtucov -- three ARM load/store translation units still have no writeback-probe row || qharmstorepre -- store pre-index writeback has no probe row || qhwalloracles -- Owed assessment of wall-clock measurement oracles and fixed execution windows, including halt-within-window gates, grace constants, and run_emu margins; transport timeouts stay with loadfragile || qharmstaleprompt -- arm_flags_probe whole-buffer waits return on the previous prompt || qharmsendstatus -- arm_flags_probe send drops the prompt-wait result || qharmreadretry -- six register, print, and copyout reads still have no consumer-keyed retry || qharmdumptail -- dump retry parsers take the first dump word in the slice || qharmretrycount -- Report retries and unparseable reads as diagnostic telemetry; do not require zero retries || qharmcolorenv -- gate_arm.sh still does not unset CLICOLOR || qhfpdefaultnote -- float_emul.c still documents the withdrawn R3010/R4010 integer default || qharmgenstore -- arm_writeback_probe.py lacks a cold general-store row || qharmgenwidth -- arm_writeback_probe.py still lacks cold general-path rows for the byte arm, the halfword alignment mask, and register-offset forms. || qharmfasthstore -- the fast store-halfword site has no probe row || qharmpathaudit -- Owed measured re-audit of the ARM translation-unit inventory, correcting four missing units to three and cross-referencing qharmtucov || qhmipsdump -- mips_rounding_probe accepts any dump-shaped line in the read slice || qhmipslong -- arc round.l, ceil.l, and floor.l still have no row || qhfpucomment -- Owed record correction of the comment that W/L stores ignore the rounding mode and that cvt.w and trunc.w are indistinguishable. || qhidlefoldloss -- The m88k idle fold is lost only for loop-head tb1 at page index zero when a .n branch ends the previous page || qhswpabort -- swp abort prints via fatal and returns without the next_ic reset || qhptyfault -- the #391 timeout detector still has no PTY-level fault injection || qhcmdresults -- sibling probe sends still drop the wait verdict || qhcmdecho -- register reads accept a bare hex line with no command echo || qhcmdabort -- A stalled pc=, step, or print is still unacted, so its late output shifts the next bare-hex read into the following register || qhcmdreaderr -- EOF and read errors are reported as timeouts || qhcmdclock -- probe deadlines use time.time || qhctrlcwait -- post-control-C wait_from results are discarded || qhdhighseed -- High-bit LDRD rows already exist, and the owed work is their mutation and sanitizer verification. || qhdwarmrows -- a warm STRD page has no row, so the fast-path chicken-out has no detector || qhdaddrrows -- LDRD and STRD register-offset and writeback rows remain owed, together with the STRD write-extent sentinel. || qhmipscensus -- Complete and record the deferred Phase-C MIPS fold census || bareflopq -- bare floppy-sized image is typed FLOPPY and no device selects that type || parsecovq -- Parser tests do not establish controller acceptance || gateorderq -- Binary withdrawal and republication, and baseline-directory producer-consumer order, still serialize the regression battery. || idlepatq -- The pinned luna88k instruction budget depends on recognizing specific guest idle patterns. || finalcountq -- SIGINT with absent or exhausted stdin blocks in the debugger before any final instruction count, while quit exits cleanly only when a command can be read. || landrateq -- landisk still has no calibrated instruction budget || logspliceq -- bracketed fatal() text can splice a guest console line || anchorevq -- Owed record correction: the anchored-regex result was measured on whole logs and does not describe streaming, which matches each assembled tail at a new position-zero boundary. || tailstepq -- Interactive confirmations ignore held stream tails || landwallq -- landisk's runaway bound is still 900 s of wall clock || canaryq -- Gate 5 ordinary rig runs still lack a standing mutant control, and gate 7 synthetic progress controls stay a separate case. || runnamesq -- Gate 5 writes and grades fixed filenames in a reusable log namespace and never checks a run identifier. || armapcovq -- The memory differential ignores real ARM subpage permission selection, grants its 1 KiB fixture access, tests mapping splits, and names both ARM and SH as producers. || qhwdcempty -- no-disk WDC commands print an unlatched debug line per command || shdmacmask -- DMATCR's transfer path masks 29 bits while the register write path keeps 24 || shdnrecords -- DN=0 comments still describe an FPU error where the manual specifies a denormal result || shfsrracite -- the FSRRA comment at cpu_sh_instr.c:3281 still says single-precision only || shszpin -- SZ1 is not assigned to bit 7 or bit 4 by either manual and has no empirical pin || shregattribution -- SH7760, CHCR_TD/CHCR_CHSET, and SH_RCR2_ENABLE comments name the wrong chip or the wrong bit || pclockdeadcode -- Owed probe hygiene: sh_pclock_probe.py keeps an unused dumped helper and duplicate landisk and dreamcast code entries. || gdromwideval -- a declined 32-bit GDROM_DATA read returns 0x0000ffff and no row pins it || gdromlatchspent -- Owed documentation, with no code change: the GDROM width warning latch is consumed before the declined store, so a later landing narrow store stays silent. || gdrom88rd -- A read of GDROM 0x88 and a write of GDROM_STAT still call fatal with no latch, and the read is the flood that was ordered filed rather than latched || wdcoddstubclaim -- row_odd_bytecount still says the harness does not stub diskimage_is_a_cdrom || gdrommaskclaim -- Owed correction of the GDROM comment that still promises a new warn site cannot reuse another site's bit, a promise the following sentences retract. || seatcopywait -- copy preserved seat logs after the panel wait || panelechocheck -- ECHO-ONLY requires both the distinctive brief line in the answer and answer-minus-brief under 800; the owed work is a harness change plus two negative controls || shfaultclause -- Owed record correction, deferred to carrier review and still owed: the member-5 clause omits that a failed SH load leaves its destination unchanged. || qhmipstlbwarn -- The optional write-time MIPS TLB-overlap debug warning remains compiled out and was left unimplemented; it is tooling, not a fidelity defect || armcpsrprint -- A direct debugger print of cpsr can show stale NZCV because the settings read does not fold the separate execution-flags field back into CPSR || pcc2lineexit -- pcctwo_interrupt_common's default still calls exit on an unsupported interrupt line, and guest reachability is unestablished || qhshelltimeout -- gate scripts still bound emulator runs with the timeout command || qhguestasan 