   "id": "armusrstop",
   "title": "cpu_arm_instr.c: a USER/SYSTEM-mode guest stops the CPU -- LDM {..pc}^ (arm_pop) and MSR SPSR_x (msr_imm_spsr) in USR32/SYS32 reach default: arms that set running = 0 (stops the current CPU; emulation ends when no CPU runs)",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": [],
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-07 from the Opus 5.5 seat's pass-1 answer on armmsrmodekill (F2 disposition 12; owner ruling 2026-10-07: FILE as its own row, not fixed in #562).  USR/SYS have no SPSR, so the architecture makes these UNPREDICTABLE; stopping the CPU is not a permitted outcome (DDI 0100I glossary: must not halt or hang).  Not yet witnessed on HEAD by a rung-3 probe.  Evidence: regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/witness_20261007/opus_pass1.md.",
