  {
   "id": "armspsrthumb",
   "title": "cpu_arm: an SPSR restore (LDM {..pc}^, DPI S-to-PC) that sets T keeps decoding ARM words until the dyntrans run loop is next entered -- the Thumb interpreter is chosen only at loop entry, arm_pop never breaks out and word-aligns the PC",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": [],
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling, from #562's §F2 pass (codex disposition 6: 'Mode filtering alone does not make applying T safe or coherent').  CORRECTED 2026-10-08 by reading the source before the round's records were written: the first filing said a restored T=1 'is not honoured' -- it IS, but late.  cpu_dyntrans.c picks arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW only at the run function's ENTRY (`if (cpu->cd.arm.cpsr & ARM_FLAG_T)`); the DPI restore breaks out (abortdyntrans_call) only for an ODD destination PC; arm_pop never breaks out and loads the PC as r[ARM_PC] & 0xfffffffc, dropping bit 1 of a Thumb address.  So after a restore that sets T the CPU can keep decoding ARM words until the loop is next entered.  Out of #562's scope (#562 declines only M[4:0]; its probe's `tbit' row pins the T BIT's provenance, not the decoder).  Not witnessed; the round owes a rung-3 attempt first.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
   "id": "armmmuvehicle",
   "title": "regress: an ARM rung-3 probe vehicle that runs a guest with the MMU ON (testarm, debugger-driven) -- the reopen condition of armthumbabortkill and the likely vehicle for armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": [],
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-07 by owner ruling: after #562, build this FIRST, then armthumbabortkill.  Open questions: does testarm's default CPU (SA1110, ARMv4) support Thumb, or is another -C cpu needed; page-table setup in guest RAM via debugger writes; translation-fault liveness control.  Test-apparatus round (witness kind harness:).  2026-10-08 agy READING (regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/agy_research_20261008.txt; facts to re-derive, not agreement): testarm default CPU SA1110; NO per-CPU Thumb capability flag -- the T bit alone selects arm_cpu_interpret_thumb_SLOW, so any -C runs Thumb; CP15 c1/c2/c3 are NOT debugger-settable -> the guest must mcr them; `put' writes VIRTUAL memory; `step' keeps working with the MMU on; minimal map = one section descriptor 0x00000c02 at a 16 KB-aligned TTB, DACR 1.  THE VEHICLE MUST MAP THE EXCEPTION VECTORS or a fault reaches cpu_dyntrans.c's 'could not find physical address of the exception handler' exit (tracked as alphaifetchkill).  Of the exits and stops agy listed on this path, these match existing rows by title: armdesc3kill, armdacr2kill, armcp15cp14exits, armendianexit, qharmexalign, alphaifetchkill.  NOT complete, and two entries were wrong as given (GPT-6 Astra, #562's confirmation): armsa1110areset is the reset alignment-control default, not the ARM_EXCEPTION_RESET exit agy listed (that exit may be unfiled), and agy's 'wfi' stop in cpu_arm_instr.c is X(reboot).",
