     "ev": "regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/grok_adversarial.txt",
     "note": "armmmuvehicle pass 1, grok's DEDICATED ADVERSARIAL job (owner: push grok) -- I'll attack the `armmmuvehicle` design the same way as the Thumb witness spec: read the brief, then hunt the source for a green report over a broken MMU fault path.The brief's fault-path claims have to be re-derived from this tree. I'll read the walk, the exception entry, and the CP15 writes next.**  It found: the coarse index >> 10 -> >> 8 and a page-masked FAR keep the rows green; 'hole dump' cannot pin c8 (the debugger invalidates on entry; perm is the row that does); Thumb LR = pc + 6 confirmed; consumer traps for armthumbabortkill / armdesc3kill / armdacr2kill."
