     "note": "VERDICT: BUILD WITH CHANGES (7) -- the design is sound and every §1/§3 claim I could test holds on a fresh build, but as written the row set is green under four of the brief's own candidate edits (c8 no-op, the coarse index shift, the DACR shift, the TTB re-resolution), its L2 table sits INSIDE its   Changes: move the L2 table out of the L1 table; pre-warm data trans so c8 is pinned (S2/S3); anchor the L2 index and in-section offsets; DACR 0x105 with the fault section in domain 2 pins the DACR shift; fall-through markers; put h WARMS too (a wrong premise); a ttb2 row.  Found: armusrwarmap (measured) and the Thumb return addresses (armthumbabtlr, measured)."
