   "id": "armmsrmodedebt",
   "title": "#562's arm_msrmode_probe.py: measured residue -- latch-CLEAR x bits 31:8 at the restores (5 escapes), msr label x latch (2), the cached ic->arg[] (M_msr_argmask), grid cov asserting G1 only -- with measured closures for the five restore-flag escapes (a session reorder) and the cached-translation mutants (a 48th loop row)",
   "sev": "LOW",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": [],
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09 by owner ruling ('commit, file the rest') from #562's final pass: the Opus 5.5 seat MEASURED the escapes (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/opus_pass2r5_20261009/KTR5_LANE1..5.out) and both closures -- the zero-observation reorder of the DPI/pop grid sessions (all five latch-clear escapes 46/47, fix 47/47; KTR5W2_*.out, probe47r.py) and the loop row (fix 48/48, M_msr_argmask 47/48, HEAD 18/48; probe48.py).  Owed together: one repair, a FULL re-table on the 48-row probe, and its own pass.  Dissent carried: deepseek, glm and kimi-k3 graded M_msr_argmask OWED; grok, codex, minimax, agy and the Opus seat graded it disclosure.  OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md carries the full entry.  Also the gate 14 parser: a dead vehicle (CONTROL=DEAD, no REDS line) is reported as malformed, and a log with one row replaced by a duplicate of another passes -- no check establishes row IDENTITY or uniqueness (the Opus seat; GPT-6 Astra's confirmation).  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1's #562 adjudication] ITEM: gate_arm.sh's `arm_msrmode rows failed` check (grep -E ' want=' | grep -cE ' FAIL ') is green only because the probe truncates notes to 64 characters, which cuts the `kill 14` note before its ' FAIL ' text; a future note edit can turn the gate RED falsely -- loud, the safe direction.  Key the check on the row's verdict column, not on free text.  ||  [2026-10-09, Fable 5.1's regress review of #562 (regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/regress_20261009/fable5_regress562.md), notes]: `tbit` and `encl2` have no diag line -- a diag_unimpl call on each is a cheap addition for THIS repair (an AST change, so not #562's); and `rows failed` is green only because note[:64] cuts kill 14's note before its ' FAIL ' text, already filed here as the gate-parser bullet.",
   "entries": []
