  {
   "id": "headerstaleobj",
   "title": "build trees: a HEADER change leaves stale objects -- the build tracks no header dependencies, propagate_all_trees.sh removes only ${F%.c}.o, and the two-part clearance ([ binary -nt source ]) cannot see an object compiled against the old header",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": "harness:#562's gate 14 run -- regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/gate14_20261009/gate14_run1.out (xscale ANCHOR_ISRC/ANCHOR_EXC red, 28/30) and gate14_20261009/xscale_ab.out: a HEAD build 30/30 twice, both incrementally rebuilt #562 builds 28/30 twice",
   "commits": [],
   "state_note": "FOUND 2026-10-09 by #562's gate 14.  #562 inserted `uint32_t mode_warned` into struct arm_cpu (src/include/cpu_arm.h) BEFORE i80321_inten/isrc, tmr0, tmr0_irq/tmr1_irq and tisr; dev_i80321.c is the only object outside src/cpus that touches them.  Every build that rebuilt only src/cpus/*.o (the carrier's recipe, my propagate562.sh and every kill-table clone) linked a dev_i80321.o compiled against the OLD layout, so the device set isrc at the old offset and the guest read 0 -- gate 14's xscale anchor red on the fix and green on HEAD, deterministically.  The two-part clearance PASSED on all three trees: the binary was newer than every source.  propagate_all_trees.sh can relink and report clearance success while header-dependent objects stay stale: `rm -f ${F%.c}.o` deletes nothing for a .h and the link recipe relinks unconditionally (GPT-6 Astra's confirmation; this note first said the tool would report the header stale -- false).  SCOPE MEASURED: only dev_i80321.c reads a field after the insertion point; cd is the last member of struct cpu, so no subsequent struct cpu member shifted, and every other non-CPU ARM access precedes the insertion; the msrmode probe drives -E testarm, which attaches no i80321, so #562's kill-table results are unaffected.  OWED: when a propagated path is a header, delete every object (or every object that includes it) and rebuild; and a third clearance part -- no object older than any edited header -- in the tool and the checkpoint step.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
   "id": "wdc473floor",
