   "title": "regress/diff_wdc_identify.c: #473's re-arm/arm clamp detector passes all 128 rows under EIGHT one-token variants (bound moves at both clamps; first-byte-only content checks), and #495's write guard is ungated",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09 from the late REVIEW seats on wdcrearmzero (Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5, both MEASURED in scratch clones; regress/artifacts/wdcrearmzero/review_20261009/).  Fable: the re-arm bound relaxed to 65536 or lowered to 16384, the arm bound relaxed to 65536, the re-arm operand swapped to atapi_received -- 0 of 128 red each; rows at 32767 and 32769 on each clamp kill all four (a just-PAST row alone cannot see a LOWERED bound).  Opus: Md_frozenj (codex's, named on #473's pass 2, never built), Md_revwalk (glm's), Md_halfj, Md_armfrozen -- every content check reads only the chunk's first byte; three rows kill all four and also HEAD with #495's write guard removed.  Clause-(d) floor breach of shipped material: L2, a FOLLOW-UP round under the late-dissent rule (disposition 2), never under #473's number.  OWNER 2026-10-09: this round FIRST, then the asiceventaddr closure, then armmmuvehicle.",
   "entries": []
