  {
   "id": "armvecrecurse",
   "sev": "HIGH",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": "",
   "title": "ARM MMU: an abort taken while the active page table does not map the vector page recurses through nested prefetch aborts until the HOST process dies (SIGSEGV after ~47,591 nested faults in 10.6 s)",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09 from the Opus 5.5 seat's armmmuvehicle pass-1 answer (MEASURED, regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/opus5/opus5_meas/meas3_base.out -- the run log, its status from waitpid -- and T3_vec_unmapped.txt, meas3.py's head-and-tail excerpt of that transcript): unmodified -E testarm, the MMU on, section 0 through a coarse table whose page 0 is unmapped, one data abort -> 47,591 nested '{ arm memory fault ...}' lines and 'Exception caused no mode change?' warnings in 10.6 s (10,473,809 bytes), the process ended by signal 11; the 'could not find physical address of the exception handler' exit in cpu_dyntrans.c appears ZERO times.  READ mechanism (Opus): arm_exception -> quick_pc_to_pointers -> the generic lookup -> translate_v2p fails -> arm_exception(PREF_ABT) -> quick_pc_to_pointers -> ... before control returns to the generic function's second lookup.  A guest that unmaps its own vectors and takes any abort ends the host process: guest-drivable process death. The unlatched fault/warning diagnostics are also a flood (floodclass).  Vehicle: armmmuvehicle.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
   "id": "sysasicbitmask31",
   "sev": "LOW",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": "",
   "title": "dreamcast_sysasicvar.h: SYSASIC_EVENT_TO_BITMASK(e) is a signed 1 << 31 for e = 31, 63, 95 -- inside the [0,95] domain SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK enforces (latent: no defined event has e & 31 == 31)",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09 from the late REVIEW seats on asiceventaddr (Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5; regress/artifacts/asiceventaddr/review_20261009/).  MEASURED: GCC yields 0xffffffff80000000, UBSan reports it (also under build-asan's flags); the ledger's recorded remedy '+ SYSASIC_EVENT_RANGE_OK(e)' is INERT (compiles at 31); the fix is 1u << ((e) & 31) with the 21 defined events' masks unchanged.  Witness: detector: (a UBSan compile-and-run row), rung 3 impossible by construction (a guest path needs a new raise site).  Provenance: the kimi substitute and codex on #466's pass 2, 2026-08-26.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
   "id": "armusrwarmap",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": "",
   "title": "ARM dyntrans: a USR-mode load or store through a host_load/host_store entry warmed by a PRIVILEGED access to the same page is served without the AP check (AP=0 under the reset S bit: user should get no access)",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1's armmmuvehicle pass-1 answer (MEASURED, sessions S8 vs S8b, regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/pass1_20261009/fable5/): in ONE step N, a privileged LDR of an AP=0 section succeeds and warms the page, MSR CPSR_c,#0x10, the same LDR in USR32 is SERVED (no abort); cold, the USR load takes the permission fault (FSR 0x0d).  cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c's fast path indexes host_load/host_store by virtual page alone and consults is_userpage only for LDRT/STRT; nothing invalidates on a mode change.  Red on HEAD, so not a vehicle row; its own round, armmmuvehicle as the vehicle, S8 as the witness shape.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
   "id": "armthumbabtlr",
   "sev": "MEDIUM",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": "",
   "title": "cpu_arm.c arm_exception(): Thumb-state aborts save the wrong return address -- data abort LR_abt = instruction + 7, prefetch abort target + 3 (DDI 0100I: + 8 and + 4 in both states)",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-09: retaddr = cpu->pc (+ 4 for a data abort) + (T ? 2 : 4), and in Thumb state cpu->pc carries bit 0.  MEASURED by Fable 5.1 on the armmmuvehicle pass-1 sessions S10 (Thumb LDR to an unmapped VA: LR_abt = 0x00008107 for an instruction at 0x8100) and S11 (Thumb BX to 0x100001: LR_abt = 0x00100003); read the same day by grok's adversarial job.  DDI 0100I A2.6.6 / A2.6.5 (ddi0100i.txt:2236, :2196) give + 8 and + 4 in both states; IRQ/FIQ are also + 4 in both (:2386, :2440), so the T ? 2 : 4 term is right only for SWI/UND.  A sibling of armthumbabortkill; reachable only with the MMU on, so after armmmuvehicle.",
   "entries": []
  },
  {
