   "id": "ofemulnodata",
   "sev": "HIGH",
   "state": "open",
   "witness": null,
   "commits": "",
   "title": "src/promemul/of.c of_emul(): the OpenFirmware emulation entry calls fatal() + exit(1) when machine->md.of_data is NULL, which is true on every machine except macppc -- and the ARM and PowerPC decoders route their OpenFirmware magic instruction to it with no machine or privilege check",
   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-16 from the adjudication of the agy pack's second readings (packet D, H1): all three seats FILE, HIGH, own row (regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/astra/D_secondreadings/codex_adjD.txt, grok/D_secondreadings/grok_adjD.txt, fable5/fable5_adj_D_secondreadings_v2_FABLE.md).  Source: prescreen_audits5.md of_two/F9.  READ at HEAD by all three: of.c:1096-1101 (the NULL check and the exit), :1078 (the only writer, of_emul_init, called only from machine_macppc.c:99); ARM decode cpu_arm_instr.c:5034-5036 -> X(openfirmware) :988-991; PowerPC decode cpu_ppc_instr.c:4400-4402 -> X(openfirmware) :3956-3958.  A guest instruction therefore ends the emulator process on machines that never set up OpenFirmware.  Not covered by ofopenexit or ofpeerexit (other sites in the same file); Fable 5.1: may share one round with them.  A rung-3 ATTEMPT exists, made by claude-opus-4-8 in the Fable seat's fallback run (so it is not a Fable ruling and owes review before it counts as the witness): regress/artifacts/adj_20261016/fable5/meas_D/witness_hostexit.py and .out, at HEAD e483d931 on the unmodified ARM test machine (the emulator prints `of_emul(): no of_data struct?' and the process exits 1), each with a benign-instruction liveness control that stays alive."
  },
