                            "date":  "2026-09-09",
                            "note":  "GPT-6 Astra @ max, scoped to the four WDC files, premise stated AS A QUESTION -- and it CORRECTED THE PREMISE, which is what that costs one clause to buy.  My \u0027no nonzero exit path\u0027 is TOO BROAD: uncaught parent exceptions (a table-integrity assert, a bad argument, a PTY or filesystem error) do exit nonzero.  What cannot is a FAILED MEASUREMENT -- \u0027neither PTY implementation propagates the child\u0027s exit status\u0027.  The gate consequence is unchanged and the sentence was false as written.  **An APPARATUS failure and a MEASUREMENT failure must not render the same.**  ACTIONABLE: wdc_altoffset_probe.py\u0027s `ok\u0027 ALREADY combines zero row failures, both breakpoint observations and full instruction-word agreement across 18 rows with explicit expectations -- \u0027a real computed decision, although it never controls exit status\u0027, so its only blocker is the single-leg question.  Ranking: CLOSEST to a contract is wdc_altoffset_probe.py, FURTHEST is wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py.  TWO FINDINGS AGAINST THE PROBES\u0027 OWN RECORDS, filed not fixed: altoffset\u0027s intro says only P2\u0027s two rows differ between legs and FOUR do (P2/s4, P2/s5, P4/t5, P4/t6); and sig_probe\u0027s `sig\u0027 oracle is NON-DISCRIMINATING -- \u0027unreadable or unrelated values also make it false, yet the output calls all those cases declined\u0027.  The omitted fourth sentinel is ALTOFF_DET_DONE.",
                            "ev":  "regress/artifacts/wiringcliff/codex_contracts_20260909.txt"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "fable5",
                            "phase":  "design",
                            "d":  "2026-09-09",
                            "date":  "2026-09-09",
                            "note":  "ADJUDICATED BY THE MAIN LOOP RUNNING AS FABLE 5.1 (owner directive 2026-09-09: \"proceed with fable for any adjudication\").  This is the adjudicator hat, not an independent seat review; it is recorded as fable5 because that is the seat the hold names.  RULING (not a held stage -- a disposition the loop had referred to the owner, now taken at the owner\u0027s direction).  A blanket re-date is REFUSED: the checker\u0027s own standard is \u0027an EXEMPTION naming the round that owes it -- debt that expires, not debt that disappears\u0027, and a re-date naming no round is the second thing.  Disposition, in three parts: (1) FILE `wdcsingleleg\u0027 -- ONE design round owing all four WDC two-leg differentials a single-leg mode AND a pass/fail contract each, wdc_altoffset_probe.py FIRST because codex found its `ok\u0027 already computes a complete verdict it merely never exits on; (2) the two CONTROLLABLE ones are decisions, so decide them: fbpending_drain_probe.py gets its EXPECT_CAP from ONE measured run (that IS the design step), and hpcmips_ctor_probe.py\u0027s home is the machine-construction gate -- codex named gate_asan_sweep.sh; VERIFY before wiring; (3) THEN re-date the four WDC entries to a date after wdcsingleleg is scheduled, each naming that round id in its reason string.  That converts the block from debt-that-disappears into debt-that-names-its-round.  All three are their own commit after #516; nothing here touches the checker today.",
                            "grader":  "main-loop (Fable 5.1)",
                            "grade":  "RULING",
                            "ev":  "regress/artifacts/wiringcliff/DERIVED_20260909.txt"
                        },
                        {
                            "seat":  "grok",
                            "phase":  "assess",
