                            "date":  "2026-09-09",
                            "grade":  "DISSENT",
                            "note":  "FILE-READING, and it VERIFIED rather than reasoned -- the strongest answer of the panel.  DISSENT on the binary split and on parts (2) and (3); part (1) upheld as one round.  Three findings, each re-verified by the loop before ruling: (i) hpcmips IS CONTROLLABLE and is \u0027the one decision this project can actually take today\u0027 -- gate_asan_sweep.sh IS the construction gate, already hosts sgi_eaddr_probe.py as a construction-time value oracle on the NORMAL binary, and hpcmips constructor deaths were already this gate\u0027s ratchet (removed from AB_EXEMPT after #444); the probe is self-contained (--binary, HPCMIPS_CTOR_PASS/_FAIL, sys.exit(main()), no rig image).  \u0027Calling it not a cheap wiring because the reason string still says wants is the correlate-not-the-property failure.\u0027  (ii) fbpending is DESIGN-blocked, not one-run: `--expect-cap` is one-sided `bD \u003c= CAP` and CANNOT distinguish a bound of 762 from 7 -- the probe\u0027s own header says so -- so one run would take N from a residue; the design step is deriving N from pending_bound/freq (dev_footbridge.c) then VALIDATING by a run.  (iii) *** THE CHECKER\u0027S OWN LIVE COMMENT ABOVE EXEMPT IS FALSE ***: \u0027These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and exits nonzero on failure\u0027 -- false of all four WDC files; a re-date that does not correct it leaves the tool asserting the claim this row just retired.  Q2: ONE round for the shared instrument change; splitting rig images into their own round \u0027invents a design that is not there\u0027 -- but the images must be in the round\u0027s OWED WORK, not merely its exemption name.  Q3: part (3) as written is debt-that-disappears for _sig and addtoinbuf; the form that expires is: when the named round ships, the exemption is DELETED in the same edit as the wiring (the pit / sh4_bsc precedent already in the checker).  fbpending and hpcmips correctly keep 2026-09-20.",
