                            "note":  "*** MEASURED 2026-09-17 BY THE OPUS 5 SEAT, ON A BATCH THAT WAS NOT ASKED ABOUT WIRING -- AND IT IS THE SHARPEST ANSWER IN THAT BATCH TO \"what is the smallest edit that breaks the fix and still passes?\" ***  For four of the nine rows reviewed, **the answer is THE ENTIRE FIX, REVERTED, and the row that stays GREEN is every row in the full battery.**     lca_confbus_probe.py      NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (lcashiftub)\n    lca_confwidth_probe.py    NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (lcaconfwidth, MED)\n    alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py  NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (alphapfnoffset, **HIGH**)\n    alpha_harness_probe.py    NOT REFERENCED BY ANY GATE    (alphaswpctxptbr, **HIGH**)\n  -- against the wired controls in the same batch: sh_iprbcd_probe.py, sgi_re_rgb_probe.py, gdrom_default_probe.py and diff_wdc_identify.c all ARE referenced.  `run.sh` runs an explicit `GATES=(...)` list and the four appear nowhere outside `regress/` and the wiring checker itself. *** TWO OF THE FOUR ARE HIGH-SEVERITY ROWS.  Delete `| (vaddr \u0026 ((1ULL \u003c\u003c pageSizeShift) - 1))` from `memory_alpha.c` and a HIGH page-walk defect is back with a CLEAN BATTERY. *** **THE SEAT EXPLICITLY DECLINED TO CLAIM THIS AS NEW, which is the right call and is why it lands here rather than as a fresh row:** `check_probe_wiring.py` already classifies all four as `CLASS_WITNESS` -- correctly, by the ladder\u0027s witness/detector timing line -- and its own entry for `lca_confbus_probe.py` says *\"but this probe RUNS IN NO GATE, so the coverage exists and is never executed: wiringcliff\"*. *** BUT THAT CHECKER IS UNCOMMITTED, so **nothing in any committed tree reports this today.** ***  The four closures are HONEST -- their `witness:` says `probe:`, which is exactly what it is -- and what is absent is STANDING DEFENCE.  The seat\u0027s disposition, adopted: this belongs in each round record as a DISCLOSED RESIDUAL on those four rows, not only as one filed id, because a reader of `alphapfnoffset` alone cannot see it."
