MR #1, #65536, #131072.  **A guest arming bit 50 at ANY moment dies within 65536 instructions, with no access in flight.**  *The seat\u0027s own first derivation said #65537 and its boundary run measured that false -- it recorded the measurement over its derivation, which is the right way round.*  STABILITY: run 1 and run 2 are BYTE-IDENTICAL across all 13 scored rows (9/13, same four FAILs), `IP30TICK_CONTROL=OK` both times.  CONTROLS ALL GREEN, including the two that make the positive attributable: **`tick49 s70k\u0027** (same store, same step count, bit 49 not 50 -\u003e alive) is the discriminator, and **`late s1\u0027** (armed AFTER tick #1 was consumed, one step -\u003e alive) is what proves `tick50 s1\u0027 measured THE TICK and not something else about the first instruction.  **L4 APPLIED TO MY OWN PROBE:** `ip30_abort_probe.py`\u0027s `acc imask\u0027 row claimed \"a handful of steps cannot reach it\".  MEASURED FALSE.  The row is still safe, for two reasons it did not state (bit 18, and `sw\u0027 cannot set bit 50 anyway), and the comment now says so.  **CONSEQUENCE FOR THE ROUND:** codex\u0027s constraint is DISCHARGEABLE rather than blocking -- the four-site closure is available because the tick row exists and is measured.  Artifacts at `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/tick_20260917/`, all four carrying their completion sentinel, copied off the volatile scratch path the measuring seat itself flagged."
