                            "grader":  "grok 4.6 xhigh, asked to WRITE the diff with the full enclosing function inlined so the sketch rule could not bite; it returned the diff plus a control-flow table and found a survive-only row that cannot see its own repair",
                            "ev":  "regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt and FIXDIFF_brief_20260917.md",
                            "note":  "*** THE FIX DIFF IS WRITTEN AND PRESERVED, AND IT FOUND A HOLE IN MY OWN DETECTOR. ***  `regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt`.  NOT APPLIED -- the adjudicated ship order puts the ip30 round LAST, after the commit and the arm probe. The diff honours every ruling: TWO latch bits (`IP30_W_TICK` 1\u003c\u003c0, `IP30_W_ISR` 1\u003c\u003c1, \u0027one bit per site, never shared\u0027), the `(once)` house marker, `break` and never an early `return` so the common tail at :180-183 still runs, the `writeflag` test at 0x10020/0x10028, and on a READ it DECLINES rather than mirroring -- *\u0027odata stays the function\u0027s 0 initializer; that is not a modelled value\u0027*.  It also declines the 0x10030 WRITE arm per the Fable ruling, with the comment *\u0027the TODO answers no.  Clearing goes through clear_isr at 0x10028\u0027*.  It carries a control-flow table showing every path lives. *** THE DETECTOR FINDING, AND IT IS FLOOR-RELEVANT: `kill 30 wr` IS SURVIVE-ONLY AND THEREFORE CANNOT SEE THIS REPAIR. ***  Post-fix the host lives on a 0x10030 write whether or not the store is applied, so an `alive` oracle is invariant under the very edit the row exists to pin.  **That row owes a STATE oracle -- write declined AND `isr` unchanged** -- which is the CHANNEL check\u0027s vacuous-by-construction shape, knowable now, before any table runs. **AND THE ISR-UNCHANGED ROW MUST COVER BOTH LOADS, with a twist at 0x10028:** `\u0026= ~0` is a no-op today, so a row that only checks the ISR CELL cannot fail there.  Pin **`odata` is not `d-\u003eisr`** instead, seeding ISR to a distinctive value first.  Without that, the 0x10028 writeflag repair ships unpinned."
