24550: ## 2026-10-09 - GXEMUL [087a90]: `#562` armmsrmodekill; what its review files
24551: 
24552: Evidence: `regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/` -- the panels (`panel_pass1_20261007` .. `panel_pass2r5_20261009`), the Opus 5.5 seat's answers and measurements (`witness_20261007/opus_*.md`,
24553: `opus_pass2*_2026100*/`), the kill tables (`killtable_20261007/` .. `killtable5_20261008/`), and agy's MMU research
24554: in `regress/artifacts/armmmuvehicle/`.
24555: 
24556: ### `armusrstop` (MEDIUM, cpu) - a USR- or SYS-mode guest stops the CPU: `LDM {..pc}^` and `MSR SPSR_x` reach default: arms that set `running = 0`
24557: 
24558: USR32 and SYS32 have no SPSR, and two guest instructions select one by switching on the CURRENT mode with no arm for
24559: them: `arm_pop`'s `^` restore (`bdt_load: unimplemented mode %i`, then `cpu->running = 0; next_ic = &nothing_call;
24560: return;`) and `msr_imm_spsr` (`msr_spsr: unimplemented mode %i`, a pc sync, then `cpu->running = 0`) -- both in
24561: `src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c`, found by `grep -n 'unimplemented mode' src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c`.  A guest reaches either
24562: from USR32 with no debugger: one `MSR CPSR_c,#0x10` (a modelled mode, accepted) and then the instruction.  The
24563: architecture makes an SPSR access from USR/SYS UNPREDICTABLE, which "must not halt or hang the processor"
24564: (`_scratchpad/ddi0100i.txt:45064`).  `running = 0` stops THIS CPU; with no other CPU running, emulation ends.  `mrs_spsr`'s
24565: `default:` is the third arm of the shape but answers 0 for USR/SYS and is reached only after a debugger `cpsr=` plant.
